 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- `POST /tickets/import` creates up to 5000 tickets in one request, all or none, for the move from the old tracker.
+
+## 1.6.0 (2026-11-15)
+
+- Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)): each ticket is due its creation time plus the response
+  time of its priority (urgent 4 hours, high 24, normal 72, low 168; `DUE_HOURS_URGENT`, `DUE_HOURS_HIGH`,
+  `DUE_HOURS_NORMAL`, `DUE_HOURS_LOW`). The due time is set once and never moves. Tickets already in the data file are
+  given theirs from their own creation time and priority the first time 1.6.0 opens it.
+- With `DUE_TIMES=on`, every ticket shows `due` and `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists the open and in-progress tickets
+  past their due time. Until then the API answers exactly as 1.4.0 does.
+- The data file stays version 1 (a ticket record gains `due`), so 1.4.0 still starts on a file 1.6.0 wrote; see
+  [operations](docs/operations.md#due-times-switching-on-and-rolling-back).
+
+## 1.5.0 (2025-10-06)
+
+- Ticket assignment: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent (or unassigns it with
+  `null`), audits the change and notifies the agent. Every ticket shows its `assignee`.
+- `GET /tickets` filters by `assignee` (`assignee=` for the unassigned). Filters now combine as documented: a ticket must
+  match every filter given, not just one of them.
+- The command-line listing shows each ticket's assignee (`list --raw` gains it as a fifth column, after the title) and
+  `list` takes `--assignee`.
+- Data files written before 1.5.0 load as they are: their tickets are unassigned.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
